# Reduced TS, step 3c: relaxed scan, HOST FROZEN VIA THE QM/MM ACTIVE REGION (C8).
#
# Step 3b used %geom Cartesian constraints to freeze the host and never
# converged. ORCA's own setup output said why:
#
#     optimized atoms = activeRegion ... 137
#     Active atoms                   ... All atoms
#     activeRegion                   ... NO
#     Choice of coordinates  ... (2022) Redundant Internals
#
# The constraints only PINNED the host; ORCA still carried all 137 atoms -- in a
# 2022-dimensional redundant-internal set -- through the step, the Hessian and
# the convergence test. So the free QM-region coordinates converged (RMS 2.9e-4)
# while the pinned host's did not (RMS 0.16, MAX 0.69), and the criterion could
# never be met. Cartesian constraints belong to a Cartesian optimization; bolted
# onto a redundant-internal QM/MM run they misbehave.
#
# The native tool is the QM/MM ACTIVE REGION: %qmmm ActiveAtoms names the atoms
# to optimise and ORCA holds everything else itself. With the 17 QM atoms active,
# `optimized atoms = activeRegion` becomes 17, not 137. ExtendActiveRegion NO
# stops ORCA adding its usual constrained shell around the active set, so only
# the QM region moves.
#
# Coordinate: forming bond O136...C129, 0-based 133 and 128 (0-based confirmed by
# the step-1 constraint echo: input 128 -> 1-based 129 = C129).
# Range 1.6 -> 2.6 A in 11 steps: brackets the maximum (seed and r2SCAN-3c TS
# both at 1.820, the r2SCAN-3c product endpoint near 1.55).
#
# Tolerances kept loose (TolRMSG 1e-3, TolMaxG 1e-2) because this scan exists to
# produce a GEOMETRY at the maximum for the OptTS to refine, not a final number.
! QM/XTB B97-3c ddCOSMO(Water) Opt TightSCF

%QMMM
QMATOMS
	{61 64 120 121 122 124 125 126 128 129 130 131 132 133 134 135 136}
END
# The atoms to OPTIMISE. Everything else is held by ORCA's QM/MM optimizer.
ActiveAtoms
	{61 64 120 121 122 124 125 126 128 129 130 131 132 133 134 135 136}
END
ExtendActiveRegion no
Charge_total 0
Mult_total 1
AutoFF_QM2_Method GFNFF
END

%geom
  Scan
    B 128 133 = 1.6, 2.6, 11
  end
  TolMaxG 1.0e-2
  TolRMSG 1.0e-3
  TolMaxD 1.0e-2
  TolRMSD 5.0e-3
  Calc_Hess true
  Recalc_Hess 50
end

%output jsonpropfile true end

%maxcore 4000

%pal
   nprocs 8
end

* xyzfile 0 1 job.xyz
